<p  ><strong >D.7 B</strong></p>
</td>
<td >
<p  >Payments for Idle Wages: In exceptional circumstances where project execution demands retention of contractor's manpower to execute the work further but due to non-availability of required inputs / fronts from BHEL / Customer and other valid reasons, payment to idle labour becomes essential, such idle wage payments would be recommended by a Committee comprising of concerned executives from the Project Site including the Head of Finance and HR at Site to Site In-charge for prior approval of Head of the Unit/ Region with the financial concurrence of Head</p>
<p  >of Finance of the Unit/ Region.</p>
<p  >&nbsp;</p>
<p  >(Note:</p>
<p  >(1) The compensation under SI. No. D.7 A, D.7 B and D.8 put together shall not exceed 15% of the contract value,</p>
<p  >&nbsp;</p>
<p  >(2) Such payment should be linked with completion of key customer requirements milestone</p>
<p  >&nbsp;</p>
<p  >(3)PSHQ shall define the admissibility and calculation criteria for Idling Wages and issue necessary guidelines)</p>
